        Root cause:
        The root cause of the bug was due to the logic implemented in a previous commit that only called `snd_soc_component_open/close()` once for each component-substream pair. This led to insufficient state tracking and improper handling of component opening failures, which resulted in PCM playback and module unload errors when components were independently opened or closed. The component opening process did not revert successfully opened components if a subsequent component failed to open, leading to resource management issues.

        Commit message:
        ASoC: soc-pcm: fix state tracking error in
